  "texts": {
    "preamble": "David Arul Raj @ David vs D.Arul Kamaraj on 25 March, 2024 Author: T.V.Thamilselvi Bench: T.V.Thamilselvi Crl.O.P.N In The High Court Of Judicature At Madras Dated : 25.03.2024 Coram The Honourable Mrs.Justice T.V.Thamilselvi Crl.O.P.No.28020 of 2022 and Crl.M.P.No.17228 of 2022 David Arul Raj @ David . Vs. D.Arul Kamaraj .. Prayer:",
    "facts": "The respondent filed a private complaint before the learned Judicial Magistrate-II, Tambaram against the petitioner for the offence punishable under Section 420 of IPC.",
    "arguments": "Further, the learned counsel for the petitioner submitted that the respondent has given a false complaint as if the petitioner involved in unlawfully activities and violated the Government order during Covid -19 even after 9.00 p.m., to 11.00 p.m., he sold the foods. Further, the learned counsel for the petitioner has relied on by Judgment in Neetu Singh & Others Vs.State of U.P. (2022 Live Law(SC) 281. 4. Inspite of notice given to the respondent, there was no representation. 5. On a perusal of the records, it reveals that the petitioner has produced the rental agreement as document on the side and also notice was issued by the Food Safety Officer but all the allegations in the petition is vexatious one. Further, the petitioner has handed over the premises to the respondent and shifted his business to other place, due to some dispute, the respondent has given a false complaint against the petitioner with some ulterior motive."
  },
